"""
build_multi_region.py

Multi-region version of distress_analysis.py. Builds ONE Excel workbook
covering both the US (ICE BofA H0A0) and EUR (ICE BofA HE00) high-yield
indices, from four source files:

    US_Index.xlsx     — current US HY index composition (one row per bond)
    US_default.xlsx   — bonds removed from the US HY index due to default
    EUR_Index.xlsx    — current EUR HY index composition (one row per bond)
    EUR_default.xlsx  — bonds removed from the EUR HY index due to default

Output workbook has FIVE sheets:

    US Index      — everything derivable from US_Index.xlsx alone: index
                     summary, rating buckets, issuer distress ranking,
                     sector exposure & CCC concentration, sector distress by
                     OAS, sector exposure by size, top 5 issuers,
                     subordination breakdown, maturity wall.
    US default    — everything derivable from US_default.xlsx alone: top
                     defaulted issuers (last 12 months) and historical
                     defaults by sector (full history).
    EUR index     — same structure as "US Index", built from EUR_Index.xlsx.
    EUR default   — same structure as "US default", built from
                     EUR_default.xlsx.
    Methodologie  — plain-language explanation of every filter, grouping,
                     and formula used, covering both regions.

Usage:
    python build_multi_region.py \
        --us-index US_Index.xlsx --us-default US_default.xlsx \
        --eur-index EUR_Index.xlsx --eur-default EUR_default.xlsx \
        --output distress_analysis_US_EUR.xlsx
"""

